.TH SURFD-SESSION 1 "October 2026" "surfd 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
surfd-session \- start the surfd desktop
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B surfd-session
.SH DESCRIPTION
Started by the login screen. Creates
.I ~/.config/surfd/surfd.toml
on first login, generates the configuration with
.BR surfctl (1)
and starts Sway. If the configuration has errors it uses the last good
generated configuration, or a minimal built-in one, and shows how to fix it.
On the proprietary NVIDIA driver it adds Sway's
.B --unsupported-gpu
option automatically.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/surfd/session.log
Output of the current session
.RI ( session.log.old
for the previous one).
.TP
.I /usr/share/surfd/fallback/sway.conf
The emergency configuration.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR surfctl (1),
.BR sway (1)
